[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The wireline: one versioned JSON payload per root, computed from the export by a backed script

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-WIRELINE
TITLE: The wireline: one versioned JSON payload per root, computed from the export by a backed script
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
wireline.py --root UID reads the strictdoc JSON export, the grammar file
and the worktree (to map a UID to its file) and writes one payload,
schema whiteboard-view/1, that the renderer and nothing else consumes.

What is in it. The tree: every narrative under the root, in Contains
order, with its fields verbatim and its STATEMENT parsed per WIDGET into
paragraphs, rows (text spans, link spans, the trailing bracket word and its
"by"), glossary terms, legend entries or table rows. The nodes: every node
the tree cites or links, with every field verbatim in grammar order, its
relations in and out, its files and its fingerprint entries. The backlinks:
for each node, which rows and which Cites point at it -- the table behind
"lines on the sheet by type", data purely in sdoc and tallied here. The
pairs: live (source type, role, target type) counts among the cited nodes,
the edges diagram's data. For each Cites: unsigned, signed or drifted (the
contract hash recomputed with the fingerprint module, imported not copied)
and whether the target is superseded. The grammar: each type's fields,
kinds and option lists, read from the grammar file because the export
types every field as String. Ladders: each choice field's option list with
a rank so a reader can order and colour badges without the grammar. And
the checks: view-check findings, count first.

Field values pass through verbatim; everything computed sits under a key
that says so. The cache key is the newest .sdoc mtime, the grammar file,
the root UID, the schema string and the script itself.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A TUI reads the same payload as the page; the payload is the contract that keeps the viewer's form open (DEC-VIEWER-FORM-UNDECIDED) while the view exists.
<<<
